---
import { DEFAULT_CONFIG, MUTE_DURATION_KEYS } from '@mutebetbot/shared';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="MuteBetBot">
  <h1>Bet your silence.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    MuteBetBot lets two members of a Discord server wager <em>time</em>, not money. Lose the bet, and the winner gets to mute
    you: {MUTE_DURATION_KEYS.join(', ')}, fixed before anyone shakes on it.
  </p>
  <a class="button" href="/invite">Add to Discord</a>

  <h2>How a bet works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <strong>Propose</strong>
      <code>/bet create</code> names your opponent, the terms, and the mute duration. Both of you click 🤝&nbsp;Accept to make it
      binding.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Settle</strong>
      When it's decided, one of you runs <code>/bet resolve</code> and the other confirms. Disagree? An admin rules.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Redeem</strong>
      The winner gets a mute token and picks <em>when</em> to use it with <code>/mute redeem</code>. Discord's own timeout does
      the rest.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Built to stay fun</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Admins cap how many people can be bet-muted at once (default {DEFAULT_CONFIG.maxConcurrentMutes}).</li>
    <li>A cooldown stops back-to-back revenge mutes, and nobody can be muted twice at the same time.</li>
    <li>The bot never shortens a moderator's timeout, and its messages can't ping <code>@everyone</code>.</li>
    <li>Admins and members above the bot can still bet: they get an <em>honor mute</em> instead.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
